      <description>📝 1 The Reset Vector &amp; Boot ROM (SecureROM) The Apple Silicon boot process begins in a state of absolute trust, anchored by the Boot ROM (often colloquially referred to as SecureROM). This code is mask-programmed into the silicon during fabrication. On recent Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3), the memory map places the Boot ROM at a high base address, typically 0x100000000.

